<title>UK: Prudential bids for Scottish Amicable. [CORRECTED 17:25 GMT]</title>
<headline>Prudential bids for Scottish Amicable. [CORRECTED 17:25 GMT]</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>British insurance company Prudential Corp said it has made a 1.9 billion pounds offer for mutually-owned life assurer Scottish Amicable, which is already the subject of a bid by bank Abbey National. (Corrects offer price from 1.5 billion to 1.9 billion.)</p>
<p>Prudential said it will pay 400 million pounds to ScotAm policyholders in the form of cash or Prudential shares and will inject 1.1 billion pounds to strengthen ScotAm's with-profits life fund.</p>
</text>
